{"document_id": "ca893acc-c451-4839-ae49-55bfd3461b2f", "crop": "mango", "organization": "Unknown", "source": "Unknown", "source_url": "https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtdieback.htm", "title": "Mango - Solutions for crop management", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-07T00:14:07.822616", "content": "  * [Skip navigation](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtdieback.htm#content)\n  * [Home](https://mango-crop.web.app/index.html)\n\n\n# ![](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/imgs/dismgtpmhdr.jpg)\n[Home](https://mango-crop.web.app/) > [Previous Page](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtdieback.htm#) > Current\n## Disease management module - Fungal\n### Bacterial & Other Diseases\nBacterial Diseases : They can cause a variety of symptoms including cankers, leaf spots, overgrowths, scabs, wilts, and others\n  * ![cancker](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/cankerleavess.jpg)\n  * ![Other](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/redrust1s.jpg)\n\n\nOthers: This disease attack can causes reduction in photosynthetic activity and defoliation of leaves thereby reducing the vitality of the host plant.\n### Fungal Diseases- Die back\nCaused by _Botryodiplodia theobromae_\nDiscoloration and darkening of bark some distance from the tip, This blackness advances\nYoung green leaves start withering – first at the base and extends outwards along the vein\n#### Fungal disease - **Die back**\n  * [ ![die-back\\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db1s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db1.jpg)![Die-back \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db1.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Die back** : Discoloration and darkening of bark some distance from the tip. This blackness advances. Young green leaves start withering – first at the base and extends outwards along the vein\n  * [ ![Die-back \\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db2s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db2.jpg)![Benalmadena \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db2.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Die back** : Discoloration and darkening of bark some distance from the tip \n\n\n  * [ ![Die-back \\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db3s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db3.jpg)![Benalmadena \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db3.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Die back** : The affected leaves turn black and roll up, Twigs/ branches die, leaves shrivel and fall, Exudation of gum is also seen. \n  * ![Benalmadena \\(larger image\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/db4.jpg) Symptoms and control !   \n**Die back** : It attacks the plant; as a result the twigs dry off. Internal discoloration is also seen on infected twigs.[![Die-back\\(thumbnail\\)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/die-back4s.jpg)](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/anthra1/die-back4.jpg)\n\n\n( Move mouse over a thumbnail for a full sized version)\n**Die back** : It attacks the plant; as a result the twigs dry off. Drying of twigs and branches followed by complete defoliation gives the tree an appearance of scorching by fire. Discoloration and darkening of the bark occurs some distance from the tip of the twigs. The dark area advances and young green leaves start withering first at the base and then extending outwards along the vein. The affected leaves turn brown and its margins roll upward. At this stage, the twig or branch dies, leaves shrivel and fall. This may be accompanied by exudation of gum. The infected twigs show internal discoloration. The association of a beetle (Xyleborusaffinis) has also known to increase the disease incidence and hence need to be controlled for disease management.  \n\n  * [Home ](https://mango-crop.web.app/index.html)\n  * [Technologies](https://mango-crop.web.app/Technologies.html)\n  * [Varieties ](https://mango-crop.web.app/var/varieties.html)\n  * [Crop production](https://mango-crop.web.app/diseasemanage/dismgtdieback.htm#)\n  * [Crop Protection](https://mango-crop.web.app/cropprotect.html)\n  * [Crop improvement](https://mango-crop.web.app/cropimprove.html)\n  * [Machineries](https://mango-crop.web.app/Technologies/machineries.html)\n  * [Contact us](https://mango-crop.web.app/ContactUs.html)\n  * Pest management\n\n\nMango crop managemnt and Diagnostic system::Developed by MK CHANDRA PRAKASH & REENA ROSY THOMAS\n", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Mango - Solutions for crop management</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"enter a brief description of your website here\">\n<meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"enter, some, keywords, seperated by, commas\">\n\n<!--STYLESHEETS-->\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/style.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/print.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"print\">\n<!--INTERNET EXPLORER SPECIFIC STYLESHEETS-->\n<!--[if lte IE 8]>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"assets/ie8_hacks.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" />\n<![endif]-->\n\n<!--Hekp IE8 and earlier with HTML5-->\n<!--[if lt IE 9]>\n<script src=\"http://html5shiv.googlecode.com/svn/trunk/html5.js\"></script>\n<![endif]-->\n\n<!--GOOGLE WEB FONTS USED IN THIS TEMPLATE - http://www.google.com/webfonts-->\n<link href=\"http://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Happy+Monkey\" rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\">\n<style type=\"text/css\">\n.auto-style1 {\n\ttext-align: justify;\n}\n.auto-style2 {\n\tcolor: #0C460C;\n}\n.auto-style3 {\n\tfont-family: Cambria, Cochin, Georgia, Times, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n\tfont-size: x-large;\n}\n.auto-style4 {\n\tfont-family: Verdana, Geneva, Tahoma, sans-serif;\n}\n.auto-style5 {\n\tfont-size: small;\n}\n.auto-style7 {\n\tcolor: #0C460C;\n\tfont-family: Tahoma;\n}\n.auto-style